<div style="font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#1c1e21;max-width:640px">
  <p>An enrollment code for unattended certificate issuance was created from a request you
  approved{{ if .ApprovedByUsername }} as <strong>{{ .ApprovedByUsername }}</strong>{{ end }}.</p>

  <p style="background:#fff6e5;border-left:3px solid #d98207;padding:10px 14px;margin:18px 0">
    The code is not in this message and never will be. It was shown once, in the terminal that ran
    <code>ssoossh service enroll</code>, and is stored nowhere else. If that terminal is gone,
    enroll again.
  </p>

  <h3 style="margin:24px 0 8px;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b7280">What it hands out</h3>
  <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px">
    <tr><td style="padding:4px 12px 4px 0;color:#6b7280;white-space:nowrap">Principal</td><td style="padding:4px 0;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">{{ .ServiceAccount }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding:4px 12px 4px 0;color:#6b7280;white-space:nowrap">Certificate life</td><td style="padding:4px 0">{{ approx .CertificateLifetime }} from each redemption</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding:4px 12px 4px 0;color:#6b7280;white-space:nowrap">Key ID</td><td style="padding:4px 0;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">{{ .KeyID }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding:4px 12px 4px 0;color:#6b7280;white-space:nowrap">Bound key</td><td style="padding:4px 0;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;word-break:break-all">{{ .PublicKeyType }} {{ .PublicKeyFingerprint }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding:4px 12px 4px 0;color:#6b7280;white-space:nowrap">Certificate options</td><td style="padding:4px 0;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">{{ if .Extensions }}{{ join .Extensions ", " }}{{ end }}{{ if .NoTouchRequired }}{{ if .Extensions }}, {{ end }}no-touch-required{{ end }}{{ if .SourceAddresses }}{{ if or .Extensions .NoTouchRequired }}, {{ end }}from={{ join .SourceAddresses "," }}{{ end }}{{ if .ForceCommand }}{{ if or .Extensions .NoTouchRequired .SourceAddresses }}, {{ end }}command={{ .ForceCommand }}{{ end }}{{ if not (or .Extensions .NoTouchRequired .SourceAddresses .ForceCommand) }}<span style="color:#6b7280;font-family:inherit">None &mdash; certificates carry the server's defaults.</span>{{ end }}</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p style="color:#6b7280;font-size:13px">
    The service account is the only principal on every certificate this code produces; your own
    username is not. The code only ever issues for that key, so a stolen code cannot be paired with
    someone else's keypair. If you do not recognize the key, expire the enrollment.
  </p>

  <h3 style="margin:24px 0 8px;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b7280">The code itself</h3>
  <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px">
    <tr><td style="padding:4px 12px 4px 0;color:#6b7280;white-space:nowrap">Valid period</td><td style="padding:4px 0">{{ datetime .ApprovedAt }} &ndash; {{ datetime .CodeExpiresAt }} <span style="color:#6b7280">({{ remaining .CodeExpiresAt }})</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding:4px 12px 4px 0;color:#6b7280;white-space:nowrap">Approved by</td><td style="padding:4px 0;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">{{ if .ApprovedByUsername }}{{ .ApprovedByUsername }}{{ if .ApprovedByEmail }} &lt;{{ .ApprovedByEmail }}&gt;{{ end }}{{ else }}<span style="color:#6b7280;font-family:inherit">not recorded</span>{{ end }}</td></tr>
    {{ if .ApprovedByName }}<tr><td style="padding:4px 12px 4px 0;color:#6b7280;white-space:nowrap">Name</td><td style="padding:4px 0">{{ .ApprovedByName }}</td></tr>{{ end }}
    {{ if .ApproverSourceIP }}<tr><td style="padding:4px 12px 4px 0;color:#6b7280;white-space:nowrap">Approved from</td><td style="padding:4px 0;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">{{ .ApproverSourceIP }}</td></tr>{{ end }}
    <tr><td style="padding:4px 12px 4px 0;color:#6b7280;white-space:nowrap">Requested from</td><td style="padding:4px 0;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">{{ .RequestSourceIP }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding:4px 12px 4px 0;color:#6b7280;white-space:nowrap">Enrollment ID</td><td style="padding:4px 0;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">{{ .EnrollmentID }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding:4px 12px 4px 0;color:#6b7280;white-space:nowrap">Request ID</td><td style="padding:4px 0;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace">{{ .RequestID }}</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p style="color:#6b7280;font-size:13px">
    The code mints certificates unattended until it expires; enroll again before then to keep the
    job running. If the approval above was not yours, say so now: the address it was approved from
    is what says whose session was used.
  </p>

  <h3 style="margin:24px 0 8px;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b7280">Setting the job up</h3>
  <p>Add this to the <code>~/.ssh/config</code> of the account that runs the job, replacing <code>/path/to/key</code> with the private key you enrolled:</p>
  <pre style="background:#f4f5f7;border-radius:6px;padding:12px 14px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.5">Match user {{ if .ServiceAccount }}{{ .ServiceAccount }}{{ else }}USERNAME{{ end }} exec 'ssoossh service retrieve --code CODE --key /path/to/key'
  IdentityFile /path/to/key
  IdentitiesOnly yes</pre>
  <p style="color:#6b7280;font-size:13px"><code>Match user</code> names the account being connected to, which is always the service account above: it is the sole principal, so ssh cannot present the certificate as anyone else.</p>
  <p style="color:#6b7280;font-size:13px">No <code>CertificateFile</code> line is needed. ssh derives the certificate's name from <code>IdentityFile</code>, so the three files must be <code>&lt;name&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;name&gt;.pub</code> and <code>&lt;name&gt;-cert.pub</code> in one directory. <code>Match exec</code> runs before ssh reads them, so this needs no agent.</p>
  <p style="color:#6b7280;font-size:13px">The certificate is refreshed when it has expired or expires within a minute. Change that with <code>--grace &lt;time&gt;</code>, or refresh unconditionally with <code>--force</code>. The code is reusable until it expires, so the same command is safe from cron or a systemd timer.</p>

  {{ if .ServerURL }}<p style="font-size:13px"><a href="{{ .ServerURL }}/service-codes/{{ .EnrollmentID }}" style="color:#1d4ed8">This code, and every redemption of it</a>.</p>{{ end }}

  <p style="margin-top:28px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb;color:#9099a8;font-size:12px">
    Sent because "Service enrollment created" is on in your
    {{ if .ServerURL }}<a href="{{ .ServerURL }}/preferences" style="color:#6b7280">notification preferences</a>{{ else }}notification preferences{{ end }},
    or because this address is set as the enrollment's notification address.
  </p>
</div>
